WEBVTT

00:12:58.357 --> 00:13:00.567
At every stage of this narrative,

00:13:00.609 --> 00:13:05.405
the health care, the transport,
the college degrees, the elderly care,

00:13:05.405 --> 00:13:08.116
we've seen universal
basic services in action.

00:13:08.116 --> 00:13:11.161
Universally available,
free at the point of consumption

00:13:11.203 --> 00:13:13.288
and paid for through progressive taxation.

00:13:13.747 --> 00:13:16.542
Now, this might sound utopian.

00:13:16.542 --> 00:13:19.336
Personally, I think
it's technically easier to do

00:13:19.336 --> 00:13:21.421
than colonizing Mars,

00:13:21.463 --> 00:13:24.007
but our society
somehow thinks differently.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.260
But it's not utopian.

00:13:26.301 --> 00:13:29.680
In fact, in many ways,
this world resembles our own.

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.474
There are still markets
for many, many things.